  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Elevated fire weather conditions (hot, dry, breezy) starting \n   today and lasting into the weekend region-wide.\n\n-  Wildfire smoke degrading air quality and reducing visibility\n   for the next several days and likely well into next week.\n\nThe region remains on the western periphery of a large-scale \nupper-level ridge. Persistent synoptic subsidence will maintain \nhot, dry, and smoky conditions through the weekend, with no \nwidespread precipitation expected.\n\nBreezy southwesterly winds today through Sunday, combined with \nlow relative humidity and hot temperatures, will result in \nelevated fire weather concerns. Red Flag Warnings are not \ncurrently planned; marginal wind speeds and relatively moist \nfuels/soil keep conditions just below warning thresholds. However,\nelevated fire weather conditions and increased fire behavior \nremain expected on existing burns or new ignitions.\n\nDeep southwesterly flow will continue transporting wildfire smoke\nfrom Washington and Oregon into Idaho and Montana, maintaining \npoor air quality and reduced visibility across the region. Despite\nhot daytime temperatures, Heat Advisories are not anticipated at \nthis time due to sufficient overnight temperature recovery and \nsmoke cover limiting peak afternoon heating.\n\nSouthwesterly flow aloft will persist through much of next week, \nmaintaining hot and mostly dry conditions alongside typical \nafternoon gusty westerly winds. Monsoonal moisture will remain \npredominantly suppressed to the south, limiting thunderstorm \npotential to occasional, slight chances across Lemhi County and \nsouthwest Montana. Given the hot and dry low level air, gusty\noutflow winds will be a concern near any thunderstorms.",
